{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9b086ff94a62973f","type":"text","text":"Does everything have to lead to a greater good? It seems like something can always be better and so maybe there's something else going on","x":-2709,"y":-400,"width":349,"height":119},
		{"id":"bcfd7871ab1c8e45","type":"text","text":"### Problem of Evil\n1. God is perfectly good\n2. The only evil that exists should bring about a greater good\n3. Unjustifiable evil exists (natural disasters - existed during Original Holiness even)\n5. God doesn't exist","x":-2979,"y":-211,"width":540,"height":214},
		{"id":"f15437df71c13f8d","type":"text","text":"### Overall Plan\nIs this really God's perfect plan? One were a vast majority of the universe will be uninhabitable unless we can travel faster than lightspeed, where life takes billions of years to emerge gradually on the planet, where God seems hidden, where suffering seems abundant?\n\nWhy did He need to create in the first place and why didn't He create something infinite or be continuously creating?","x":-3560,"y":-281,"width":484,"height":268},
		{"id":"97814f657c9be4b1","type":"text","text":"### Problem of Non-resistant Non-believers\n1. If God exists, non-resistant non-believers do not\n2. Non-resistant non-believers exist\n3. God doesn't exist\n\nAlso, if whether someone goes to Heaven is determined at their death, their death is sometimes decided by arbitrary reasons so is whether someone goes to Heaven decided somewhat arbitrarily?","x":-3318,"y":191,"width":500,"height":254},
		{"id":"7ad6c3bb6b0b9e4e","type":"text","text":"### Original Sin\nWhat changed with Original Sin? And how does it propagate to all of us and how does Baptism fix it? Why is childbirth now painful, etc.","x":-2709,"y":580,"width":407,"height":160},
		{"id":"229564b1aa1cb465","type":"text","text":"### Divine Hiddenness\nWhy does God hide Himself?\n\nSurely He has the ability to convince anyone that He exists, and if so why doesn't He do that? He was fine doing that for the Angels so why not us?","x":-2684,"y":203,"width":357,"height":231},
		{"id":"ebc2f672c53b6af8","type":"text","text":"## Deistic Hypothesis\n1. God is a necessary being, and has certain properties\n\t1. Enough power to jump start the universe\n\t2. The ability to use that power\n\nThis God is very basic and fundamentally non-refutable. This hypothesis is similar to the I Don't Know Hypothesis. The Universe was created, but this hypothesis says nothing about overall purpose or properties of the universe","x":-934,"y":-305,"width":570,"height":265},
		{"id":"0161438cd5dd4de7","type":"text","text":"This might lead to Catholicism, since if God is assumed then miracles have higher evidential power","x":-1360,"y":-67,"width":361,"height":97},
		{"id":"87dc04aec009211c","type":"text","text":"## Other Religions\nehh probably false","x":-1360,"y":-320,"width":279,"height":120},
		{"id":"0bde107431262d60","type":"text","text":"## I Don't Know Hypothesis\n1. Whatever axioms are necessary for the laws of physics are necessary things\n\nThe laws of physics are all that's needed to explain everything starting from the big bang\n\nWhy are these axioms necessary? Nobody knows","x":-240,"y":-360,"width":600,"height":206},
		{"id":"04f1b6e132343bde","type":"text","text":"Essentially has the same results as other atheistic hypothesis. It does get around arguments against arguments for the cause of the Universe, although its kinda cheap","x":20,"y":-40,"width":300,"height":162},
		{"id":"8ebd4cf785adde60","type":"text","text":"# No","x":440,"y":-572,"width":120,"height":60},
		{"id":"5703a1e52e289455","type":"text","text":"### Gradual Revelation\nSlavery was allowed in the Bible, and some rules set by Moses were later overturned by Christ. Revelation itself has been gradual through prophets and eventually Christ.\n\nWhy is the development of revelation and our understanding of morality shifting over the years and not just told to us from the beginning?\n","x":-1484,"y":235,"width":394,"height":285},
		{"id":"33c9ee05bd7a8943","type":"text","text":"### Necessary Things\nAxiomatic systems seem to be a necessary thing, Say God didn't exist wouldn't Math still exist?","x":-840,"y":80,"width":457,"height":132},
		{"id":"8baf9577769b2ac5","type":"text","text":"## In Brief\nCCC 44-49\n- Man is by nature and vocation a religious being. Coming from God, going toward God, man lives a fully human life only if he freely lives by his bond with God.\n- Man is made to live in communion with God in whom he finds happiness: When I am completely united to you, there will be no more sorrow or trials; entirely full of you, my life will be complete (St. Augustine, _Conf_. 10, 28, 39: PL 32, 795).\n- When he listens to the message of creation and to the voice of conscience, man can arrive at certainty about the existence of God, the cause and the end of everything.\n- The Church teaches that the one true God, our Creator and Lord, can be known with certainty from his works, by the natural light of human reason (cf. Vatican Council I, can. 2 § 1: DS 3026),\n- We really can name God, starting from the manifold perfections of his creatures, which are likenesses of the infinitely perfect God, even if our limited language cannot exhaust the mystery.\n- Without the Creator, the creature vanishes (_GS_ 36). This is the reason why believers know that the love of Christ urges them to bring the light of the living God to those who do not know him or who reject him.","x":-660,"y":339,"width":909,"height":410},
		{"id":"13c9aca1072f8f09","type":"text","text":"## God's Omniscience\nPsalm 139:4\n- Even before a word is on my tongue, O Lord, you know it completely\nIsaiah 46:9-10\n- I am God, and there is no one like me, declaring the end from the beginning and from ancient times things not yet done, saying, \"My purpose shall stand, and I will fulfill my intention\"\nCCC 600\n- To God, all moments of time are present in their immediacy. When therefore he establishes his eternal plan of \"predestination\", he includes in it each person's free response to his grace\n","x":-340,"y":860,"width":660,"height":342},
		{"id":"889817686bd1a7ed","type":"text","text":"## Speaking about God\nCCC 40\n- Since our knowledge of God is limited, our language about him is equally so. We can name God only by taking creatures as our starting point, and in accordance with our limited human ways of knowing and thinking.\nCCC 42\n- God transcends all creatures. We must therefore continually purify our language of everything in it that is limited, image-bound or imperfect, if we are not to confuse our image of God — \"the inexpressible, the incomprehensible, the invisible, the ungraspable\" — with our human representations. Our human words always fall short of the mystery of God.","x":452,"y":600,"width":691,"height":366},
		{"id":"49acbe0d9128d7c5","type":"text","text":"## Multiverse Hypothesis\n1. Everything that is self contained exists\n2. Perhaps some things like axiomatic systems always exist no matter what\n\nThe observable universe is something that appears to be self contained, and hence exists. Conscious creatures like us are very unlikely to occur, but necessarily will because consciousness is not logically contradictory","x":560,"y":-413,"width":582,"height":216},
		{"id":"c0507b61f56f1a2b","type":"text","text":"### Explain the beginning of the Church\nWhether or not He was God, Jesus of Nazareth is the historically most important person in human history. Why is that if He was a fraud?","x":500,"y":75,"width":420,"height":157},
		{"id":"f47d903f35d80677","type":"text","text":"### Cosmological Argument\n1. The Universe had a beginning\n2. Everything that has a beginning has a cause\n3. The Universe had a cause that can't be from the universe (timeless, spaceless)","x":1317,"y":-413,"width":420,"height":191},
		{"id":"3d4b2f79f6c37930","type":"text","text":"# Does God exist?","x":-330,"y":-860,"width":260,"height":60},
		{"id":"645429fe57d34104","type":"text","text":"Obviously no one knows for sure whether God exists. Even \"knowing\" something is an assumption. However, for practical purposes it makes sense to assume the following otherwise you will get nowhere:\n1. Logic and Reason are valid","x":-499,"y":-740,"width":599,"height":154},
		{"id":"79958d5da1011e9d","type":"text","text":"# Yes","x":-883,"y":-542,"width":130,"height":60},
		{"id":"aa50f50584dccb41","type":"text","text":"### Scriptural Contradictions\nScripture contradicts itself multiple times, why is this the case?\n\n1. put examples here\n","x":-2267,"y":235,"width":360,"height":165},
		{"id":"ac8a1fc198c92ec6","type":"text","text":"## Catholic Hypothesis\n1. God is a necessary being, and has certain properties\n\t1. Has a will (def. non deterministic and non random)\n\t2. All knowing\n\t3. All powerful\n\t4. All good\n\nUsing His will and power, God creates something which He knows will bring about the most good (maybe not actually)\n\nThis creation is the Universe and we were made in the image and likeness of God (have a will) and are destined to be in communion with God in Heaven","x":-2143,"y":-341,"width":659,"height":350},
		{"id":"e3d847c54e77f73e","type":"text","text":"### Teleological Argument\nThe universe appears fine tuned for our existence, odds are it was made for us","x":1280,"y":-160,"width":320,"height":140},
		{"id":"1c09be9036e7a75d","type":"text","text":"### Evidential Argument\nSupernatural unexplainable things seem to have and continue to occur\n\nThe Shroud / Our Lady of Guadalupe\nEucharistic Miracles - look at map","x":1000,"y":44,"width":349,"height":220},
		{"id":"7fa66e9677938044","type":"text","text":"Happy Guilt???","x":1271,"y":633,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c2aa8c30d52ca125","type":"text","text":"### Strange Facts\nA person's belief can be statistically predicted based on their geographic location of birth and their parents religion. Basically people fit in with religion on average just like many other things in life","x":-2267,"y":600,"width":388,"height":192},
		{"id":"45e1664cd0eed738","type":"text","text":"### Role of the Soul\nfrom psychedelics and brain injuries it appears that physical changes to the brain results in changes in consciousness, so how would consciousness be separate/have an independent entity?\n\nBasically what is the role of the soul?","x":-1860,"y":235,"width":320,"height":311},
		{"id":"3943894a2763177c","type":"text","text":"# Maybe","x":-278,"y":-542,"width":157,"height":60}
	],
